|name = Dark Otter
|image = E 124.png
|first appearance = '''SoL''': [[Claustronyctophobia|Sub-chapter 21 - Claustronyctophobia]]<br>
'''ItF''': [[Colombia (Into the Future)|Chapter 2 - Colombia]]<br>
'''Aku Realms''': [[Spain (Aku Realm)|Spain/Aichi]]
|latest appearance = '''ZL''': [[Yodoyo Sea|Sub-chapter 13 - Yodoyo Sea]]
|money drop = 250¢ - 988¢
}}

==Enemy==
Dark Otter is a lot stronger than his predecessor, having about 4x the attack and about 6x HP the health of a normal [[Otta-smack-u]]. His range is marginally higher, and he has two knockbacks instead of one. Unlike most other [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark Enemies]], he has a low money drop and can take a massive punch before being knocked back once, somewhat acting as a tanker.

==Strategy==
Because of his extreme stats, it is recommended to use meatshields like [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Macho Cat]] and [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Wall Cat]], and stack up attackers like [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]] and [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]]. [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Weightlifter Cat]] works the best for this enemy. [[Onmyoji Cat (Rare Cat)|Magica Cat]] is another option to keep pushing him away from your cats; or even better, [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]]. Any of the [[Sengoku Wargods Vajiras (Gacha Event)|Sengoku Wargods]], due to their anti-Dark abilities, will make Dark Otter easier to deal with.

