==Trivia==
*His Japanese name, Burakko, is a portmanteau of ''burakku'', meaning "black", and ''rakko'', meaning "sea otter".
*The ''[[wikipedia:Umeboshi|umeboshi]]'' mentioned in his Japanese description is a pickled or dried ''ume'', a species of apricot.

